# Backend hosting

- **Backend + database = self-hosted Convex on Openship VPS**, not Convex Cloud.
- Live URLs: `https://convex.poscalfx.com` (API) and `https://convex-http.poscalfx.com` (HTTP actions).
- Openship project: **Convex** (`proj_BbrTJLgas6VNS-B4`).

## Deploying Convex functions (correct way)

From the Poscal repo, point the CLI at the VPS (never cloud deploy keys):

```bash
# in .env.local (do not commit)
CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_URL=https://convex.poscalfx.com
CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_ADMIN_KEY=<admin key from VPS>

npx convex deploy
```

Generate/rotate the admin key on the VPS Convex backend container, e.g.:

```bash
docker exec <convex-backend-container> ./generate_admin_key.sh
```

- Do **not** use `CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY` / cloud `npx convex deploy` against `*.convex.cloud`.
- Do **not** mix cloud and self-hosted env vars in the same shell.
- Frontend app (Poscal) deploys via Openship git deploy / Vercel as configured; that is separate from pushing Convex functions.
